    narr:narration """In this discussion, [the facilitator initiates the review of the migration cutover plan](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_2) and [requests feedback on operational staffing impacts](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_3). The proposed model specifies [sequential cutovers with soak periods between sites](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_7). In response, [the operations lead endorses the single-site sequence](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_9), explaining that [concurrent cutovers would overwhelm supervisory capacity across the region](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_11) and [represent an impossible staffing requirement](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_12). This framing presents [the staffing constraint as non-negotiable arithmetic](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_14), which [the technical contributor acknowledges as a definitive hard constraint](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_15). Additionally, [the operations lead highlights cross-site supervisory learning](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_18), while clarifying that [the staffing limit remains the primary justification](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_22). [The technical contributor confirms technical architectural assumptions require single windows](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_25). Finally, [the operations lead requests early scheduling and protected soak durations](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_28), which [the facilitator commits to upholding](https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_29).""" ;
